>  2. How in the world is encumberance computed for this game???  I've
>found that Barbarians w/ STR of 18 or higher seem to get BURDENED by
>carrying little beyond a weapon and armor, whereas Samurai w/ STR of 16
>or so seem to be able to carry a lot more before they start getting
>BURDENED.  I've seen this many times while carrying nearly identical
>items with both classes.  (Could it be that barbarians aren't supposed
>to wear armor beyond leather, like in the Advanced Dungeons and Dragons
>"Unearthed Arcana" version?)  I haven't analyzed this feature for the
>other classes yet...

Nethack has little to do with AD&D rules - AD&D rules are only vague 
guidelines for code. At any rate...you get what you pay for. Couldn't
tell you much about Sam's, having only played 3 recently (rather worthless
pieces of crud, too - definitely can't do the "tank" barbarian style
fighting with them =)...but if you wear any kind of plate, that's pretty
damned heavy and that'll burden you down if you do much more than carry
a weapon...at least at *first*. I may be wrong, but I think carrying
capacity goes up somewhat (don't ask me how much, I dunno) the more you
rise in levels. Also, any dragon scale mail is damned heavy stuff. 'S
why I generally shun GDSM as a wish or present until I'm getting down to
the heavy levels.

Your *best* bet for commonly found armor is dwarvish mithril coats.
They're pretty light, and give you an AC of -6 for a +0 suit (DSM gives
you -9). That's as good as you're going to get without having to start
worrying about weight.

Even when you have gauntlets of power, if you're lugging around too much,
you're going to have a strain. (which is why many people leave their gold
behind, and consequently have lower scores when they buy the farm...=).
That's "real" life, not "I have a barbarian with a 25 str who is 
lugging around 169,783,212 pieces of gold in a bag of holding..." =)

